{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.GZWeightGeneral","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZWeightGeneral","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZWeightGeneral.fiveTwo_half_integer_needs_trivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZWeightGeneral.fiveTwo_half_integer_needs_trivial","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZWeightGeneral.lean#L108-L118","doc":"**`5₂`: `±3/2` needs the trivial connection.** Any `5₂` Stokes ray carrying the\nhalf-integer weight `±3/2` must have `sigma0` as an endpoint — never the\ngeometric–conjugate A_ω ray. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZWeightGeneral.fiveTwo_weightDiff_aomega_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZWeightGeneral.fiveTwo_weightDiff_aomega_zero","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZWeightGeneral.lean#L99-L106","doc":"**`5₂` A_ω ray has integer exponent `b = 0`.** The geometric saddle and its\nconjugate are both non-trivial, so the `5₂` A_ω (geometric ↔ conjugate) ray has GZ\nweight difference `0 ∈ ℤ` — certifying that the extracted `Ind^{rot}_{5₂}` is a genuine\ninteger Stokes datum, exactly as the merged `4₁` `weightDiff_aomega_zero`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZWeightGeneral.instDecidablePredFiveTwoConnFiveTwoTrivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZWeightGeneral.instDecidablePredFiveTwoConnFiveTwoTrivial","kind":"instance","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZWeightGeneral.lean#L96-L97","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZWeightGeneral.fiveTwoTrivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZWeightGeneral.fiveTwoTrivial","kind":"def","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZWeightGeneral.lean#L91-L94","doc":"Triviality predicate on the `5₂` connections: only `sigma0` is trivial. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZWeightGeneral.instDecidableEqFiveTwoConn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZWeightGeneral.instDecidableEqFiveTwoConn","kind":"instance","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZWeightGeneral.lean#L87-L87","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZWeightGeneral.FiveTwoConn.realSaddle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZWeightGeneral.FiveTwoConn.realSaddle","kind":"ctor","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZWeightGeneral.lean#L86-L86","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZWeightGeneral.FiveTwoConn.conjugate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZWeightGeneral.FiveTwoConn.conjugate","kind":"ctor","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZWeightGeneral.lean#L85-L85","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZWeightGeneral.FiveTwoConn.geometric","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZWeightGeneral.FiveTwoConn.geometric","kind":"ctor","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZWeightGeneral.lean#L84-L84","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZWeightGeneral.FiveTwoConn.sigma0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZWeightGeneral.FiveTwoConn.sigma0","kind":"ctor","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZWeightGeneral.lean#L83-L83","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZWeightGeneral.FiveTwoConn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZWeightGeneral.FiveTwoConn","kind":"inductive","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZWeightGeneral.lean#L76-L87","doc":"The flat connections of `5₂` carrying the resurgent structure: the **trivial**\nconnection `sigma0`, and the three non-abelian saddles of the cubic trace field\n`ℚ(ξ)`, `disc = −23` (one **real** saddle, and the **geometric** saddle with its\ncomplex **conjugate** — the `disc < 0` `1+2` splitting). The GGM Stokes matrices\n`S±(q)` are `3×3` over the three non-trivial saddles; the `(σ₁,σ₁) = (geometric,\ngeometric)` diagonal entry is the rotated index `Ind^{rot}_{5₂}` (eq. 102). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZWeightGeneral.weightDiffGZ_half_integer_needs_trivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZWeightGeneral.weightDiffGZ_half_integer_needs_trivial","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZWeightGeneral.lean#L62-L72","doc":"**A half-integer exponent forces a trivial endpoint.** `b = ±3/2` can occur only\non a `σ₀ ↔ (non-trivial)` ray. So the geometric–conjugate A_ω ray (both non-trivial)\ncan *never* carry `±3/2` — the `β = 3/2` category error, in knot-independent form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZWeightGeneral.weightDiffGZ_eq_zero_of_both_nontrivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZWeightGeneral.weightDiffGZ_eq_zero_of_both_nontrivial","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZWeightGeneral.lean#L53-L60","doc":"**Both endpoints non-trivial ⇒ integer exponent `0`.** The A_ω-type ray\n(geometric ↔ conjugate, both non-trivial) has weight difference `0 ∈ ℤ` for *every*\nknot — so its Stokes constant is an integer (the DT/BPS rotated `3d`-index, GGM\nConj. 2), never a half-integer-weight modular datum. Knot-independent. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZWeightGeneral.weightDiffGZ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZWeightGeneral.weightDiffGZ","kind":"def","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZWeightGeneral.lean#L45-L49","doc":"The **Borel characteristic exponent** of a Stokes ray joining `σ, σ′` is the GZ\nweight difference `b = κ(σ) − κ(σ′)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZWeightGeneral.kappaGZ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZWeightGeneral.kappaGZ","kind":"def","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZWeightGeneral.lean#L37-L43","doc":"**Knot-independent GZ automorphy weight.** For any connection type with a\n`trivial`-connection predicate, `κ(σ) = 3/2` iff `σ` is trivial, else `0` (GZ eq. 3.7).\nThe `3/2` is the Kashaev `N^{3/2}`-prefactor exponent — universal across knots, indexed\nonly by triviality of the flat connection. ","signatureChunk":0}]}